+ * or the anchor in @recover_slot. A frame refreshes the chain slot, plus a
+ * free (or the oldest) anchor slot when @want_anchor. A recovery frame
+ * refreshes the chain slot too, so the slot the decoder may hold stale is
+ * overwritten by the first frame it receives, and the anchor stays held for
+ * a second recovery. Anchors newer than the recovery anchor may be missing
+ * in the decoder: they are forgotten, and their slots returned to be cleared
+ * from the VBI before the frame is coded.
